  "question": {
    "text": "The standard electrode potential (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>) for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Cr</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Mn</mi></math> &amp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Co</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>41</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>57</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>97</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, respectively. The metal ions which can liberate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;from a dilute acid are",
